## English

### 1. Introduction

This Privacy Policy explains how the Android app "HomeAlarm" (the "App") handles
information. The App provides alarms that ring only while you are at home.

### 2. Location

The App uses the location permission **solely to determine whether you are at home**.

**What is accessed**
On Android, reading the name (SSID) and access-point identifier (BSSID) of the
Wi-Fi network the device is connected to requires location permission. The App
accesses **only this connected Wi-Fi information**. It does not obtain
latitude/longitude via GPS.

**When it is accessed**
- Just before an alarm rings, to check for a few seconds whether the device is
  connected to your registered home Wi-Fi (this happens while the app is in the
  background, which is why "Allow all the time" location access is required)
- While the app is open on screen, to show the at-home status
- When you register your home Wi-Fi

**How it is used and stored**
- The obtained Wi-Fi name is used **only to compare** against the home Wi-Fi you registered
- Only the registered home Wi-Fi name (SSID/BSSID) is stored, and **only in a
  database on your device**
- Location and Wi-Fi information is **never transmitted off your device**
- No movement or behavioral history is recorded

**Deletion**
You can delete registered home Wi-Fi entries at any time from the in-app Settings.
Uninstalling the App removes all data from your device.

### 3. Advertising (Google AdMob)

The App shows ads served by Google AdMob to remain free. For ad delivery,
Google may collect:

- Advertising ID
- Device information such as IP address, device model, and OS version
- Ad impression and interaction data

This information is collected and processed by Google, not by the developer. See:

- Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
- Google Ads Settings: https://adssettings.google.com
- How Google uses data in AdMob: https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543

You can reset your Advertising ID or opt out of ad personalization in your
device settings (Privacy > Ads).

### 4. Data you enter

Alarm names, times, repeat days, and ring/skip history are stored **only on your
device** and are never transmitted externally.

### 5. Data collected by the developer

The developer does **not** transmit or collect any personal information to any
server of their own.

### 6. Children's privacy

The App is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect
personal information from children.

### 7. Changes to this policy

If this policy changes, this page will be updated. Material changes will be
announced in the app or on the store page.

### 8. Contact

For questions about this policy, contact read.red.rat@gmail.com.
